property.value:
■ At the end of your opponent's turn, if your opponent has at least 4 or more creatures than you do and you have no 'Blue Impulse', you may summon this creature for no cost.
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
{SMASH BURST} (Whenever this creature attacks, you may cast its spell side in the battle zone for no cost.)

■ Galaxy Vortex evolution: Put this card on top of 3 of your Zombie Dragon, Armored Dragon or Earth Dragon creatures.
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Meteorburn: Whenever this creature attacks, you may put a creature under this creature into your graveyard. If you do, put a non-evolution Dragon from your hand, choose one of your opponent's creatures that has power 5000 or less and destroy it, then choose a card from your opponent's mana zone and put it into its owner's graveyard.

■ At the start of your turn, you may return this creature from your mana zone to your hand.
{QUATTRO BREAKER}
■ When you put this creature or another creature that has power 12000 or more, put the top 2 cards of your deck into your mana zone, then return a creature from your mana zone to your hand.

■ Galaxy Vortex evolution: Put on top of 3 of your Armored Dragon, Tyranno Drake or Brave Spirit creatures.
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Meteorburn: Whenever this creature attacks, you may put a card under this creature into your graveyard. If its a non-evolution creature, put it from your graveyard. That creature gets "speed attacker" until the end of the turn. Destroy that creature at the end of this turn.

{GUARDMAN} (You may tap this creature to change the attack target of your opponent's creature from your other creatures to this creature.)
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Your creatures that have power 12000 or more can't leave except by losing a battle.

■ Neo Evolution: You may put it on one of your creatures.
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Whenever this creature attacks, look at the top 3 cards of your deck. From among them, put any number of neo creatures and put the rest on the bottom of your deck in any order.

■ Neo Evolution: You may put it on one of your nature creatures.
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Whenever you put a creature, you may put a nature creature that has power 12000 or more that costs 1 less than that creature from your mana zone.

{TRIPLE BREAKER}
TWINPACT
■ Put the top card of your deck into your mana zone.

■ Ura Ninja Strike 3 (Nature) (Whenever one of your opponent's creatures attacks or blocks, if you have 3 or more cards in your mana zone and at least one of them is a nature card and if during that attack you didn't use a "Ninja Strike" ability, you may summon this Shinobi for no cost. At the end of that turn, put this Shinobi on the bottom of your deck.)
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ When you put this creature, choose a creature. This turn, that creature gets +4000 power and can't attack players.

■ Evolution: Put on one of your Phoenix creatures.
{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ Meteorburn: Whenever this creature attacks, you may put a card under this creature into your graveyard. If it's the last card under this creature and it was a Phoenix, you win the game.

■ Evolution: Put on one of your Cyber creatures.
{DOUBLE BREAKER}
■ When you put this creature, you may return any number of your non-evolution Cybers from the battle zone to your hand. Then for each creature returned in this way, you may put a non-evolution Cyber creature from your hand.

{TRIPLE BREAKER}
■ When you put this creature, you may choose one of your creatures and one of your opponent's creatures. Those 2 creatures battle.
■ Whenever a non-dragon creature would be put into the battle zone, put it into its owner's graveyard instead.

{DOUBLE BREAKER}
■ When this creature would be discarded from your hand during your opponent's turn, you may put it instead. If you do, you may choose a creature and return it to its owner's hand.
■ Whenever you use a "Ninja Strike" ability of your Shinobi, you may draw a card.
